---
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   / — the offer: a free 45-minute session, and one written recommendation.

   THE CALL IS THE PRODUCT, THE REPORT IS WHAT YOU LEAVE WITH. Earlier versions
   led with a researched analysis and made the call the follow-up. That sold a
   document, and a document that lands in an inbox and hopes was the weakest
   joint in the funnel. This page leads with the session — what it is, why a
   leader should take it, what they get out of it — and the report arrives
   shortly after, as the written form of the one thing we would do first.

   ONE BIG THING, NOT A MENU. The report is a single recommendation with the
   evidence behind it: what we would build, why now, what we would refuse to
   build, and the one thing we could not see from outside. Two findings is a
   menu; one is a position. The page promises exactly that shape.

   ONE WAY IN. "Book the call" lands on the questions; the calendar is on the
   confirmation screen. A book-first path existed for a week and was cut on
   2026-09-02: two entrances to one form was one more decision than the page
   needed to ask.

   NO SCORING ON THIS PAGE, AND NONE BEHIND IT. Every lead sees the calendar
   and every lead is researched. The team reads the alert and decides.

   THE COPY NARRATES NOTHING ABOUT HOW THE REPORT IS MADE. What the pipeline
   does, who reads what, and how long a review takes are ours to worry about.
   The visitor is told what they get and when: shortly after the call.

   Positioning: written to the recommended position in docs/01 — design-led AI
   product studio with a care-operations wedge — and deliberately naming no
   vertical, so landing Decision #1 does not invalidate the page.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';

const title = 'A free 45-minute session, and the one thing to build first - SeeSaw Labs';
const description =
  'Forty-five minutes with the people who would build it. We research your business before we meet, and shortly after the call you get one written recommendation: what to build first, why now, and how we would do it. Free.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- ------------------------------ hero ------------------------------ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__in">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free · 45 minutes with the team · One written recommendation</p>
      <h1 class="hero__h">
        Forty-five minutes with the people who&rsquo;d build it.<br />
        <span class="hero__em">Then the one thing to do.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede hero__lede">
        A working session, not a sales call. We research your business before we
        meet, open with what we found, and put the few questions to you that
        change the answer. Shortly after, you get a concise report: the one
        thing we&rsquo;d build first, why now, and how we&rsquo;d do it.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a href="#request" class="btn">Book the call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------------------------- what it is -------------------------- -->
  <section class="section" id="what">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Three things, and all of them are free</h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="cards">
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">The call</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            Forty-five minutes with the team that would do the work. We&rsquo;ve
            done the homework, so the first five minutes are our read of your
            business and the rest is you correcting it. No twenty minutes of
            background, no deck.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">The report</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            One recommendation, in writing, shortly after we talk. What
            we&rsquo;d build first and what it would take, why the timing is
            now, how we&rsquo;d tackle the problem, and the things we
            couldn&rsquo;t see from outside.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card__h">The people</h3>
          <p class="card__b">
            You talk to the designers and engineers who would ship it, not a
            salesperson. If there&rsquo;s no fit, we say so inside the 45
            minutes rather than in a follow-up sequence.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------------------------- why do it --------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--sunk" id="why">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why take it</p>
      <h2 class="h2">
        Everyone&rsquo;s telling you to do something with AI. Almost nobody will
        tell you <em>which</em> thing.
      </h2>
      <p class="body">
        If you run a business right now you have four questions, and they are
        hard to get straight answers to: What is actually working in my category,
        and what is theatre? If I build the thing, what does it really cost and
        how long does it take? Where have companies my size wasted money on
        this? And what should I do first - and what should I leave alone?
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        Those are the questions the call is built to answer and the report is
        built to write down. Not a list of possibilities. One position, taken by
        people who have shipped this kind of work and have watched the expensive
        versions fail, with the reasoning in the open so you can disagree with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ----------------------------- how it works ----------------------- -->
  <section class="section" id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 class="h2">The discovery process, start to finish</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          This is the same first step we take on paid engagements. You get to
          see it before deciding whether to work with us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step">
          <h3 class="step__h">Answer a few questions, then book</h3>
          <p class="step__b">
            Tell us who you are and what you&rsquo;ve already tried, then pick a
            time on the calendar. The questions take under three minutes and
            they aim the research.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <h3 class="step__h">We research before we meet</h3>
          <p class="step__b">
            What comparable companies have actually shipped and when, what
            your category is searching for, and the regulatory and funding
            movement around it. We arrive having read the industry, not just
            your homepage.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <h3 class="step__h">The 45 minutes</h3>
          <p class="step__b">
            We open with our read. You tell us where it&rsquo;s wrong. Then we
            put the handful of questions to you whose answers change the
            recommendation - the ones only someone inside the business can
            answer. You leave knowing what we&rsquo;d do first and what we&rsquo;d
            park.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <h3 class="step__h">Shortly after: the report</h3>
          <p class="step__b">
            One thing to build, in writing, with the evidence. What it is, why
            now, what it would take, and where we might still be wrong. Yours
            to keep and to socialize around your org.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <h3 class="step__h">Then it&rsquo;s your call</h3>
          <p class="step__b">
            If the thing is worth building and we&rsquo;re the right people, we
            say what it would take and get moving. If it isn&rsquo;t, or we
            aren&rsquo;t, we say that instead. Nothing here obliges you to
            anything.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------ working with us ------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--sunk" id="us">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What it&rsquo;s like to work with us</p>
        <h2 class="h2">The same discipline we&rsquo;d bring to the build</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="two">
        <div>
          <p class="body">
            Every number in your report either links to the source we found it
            in, or is an assumption we state with the reasoning attached. Where
            only you can know the figure, it stays a
            visible <span class="blankdemo">blank</span> rather than a
            confident guess. That is enforced, not just intended: a claim we
            cannot trace never reaches you.
          </p>
          <p class="body">
            We tell you what not to build. Most of what makes AI work at a
            company like yours is sequencing something unglamorous first -
            a record nobody keeps, a data path that doesn&rsquo;t exist yet. When
            that&rsquo;s the honest answer, it&rsquo;s the answer we give, even
            though it&rsquo;s worse for us.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="body">
            We are a design-led AI product studio. We build things people use,
            with the people who will use them, in operations-heavy businesses
            where the product is somebody&rsquo;s judgement. The platform that
            cut medication approvals 5x at Hospice Pharmacy Solutions is ours,
            and so are the lessons from the pilots we&rsquo;ve watched die in
            security review.
          </p>
          <p class="body">
            Reasoning in the open, assumptions labelled, one position rather
            than a menu. If that&rsquo;s how you&rsquo;d want a team to work
            once money is involved, the 45 minutes is a free look at it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------------ request ---------------------------- -->
  <section class="section" id="request">
    <div class="wrap">
      <IntakeForm />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ------------------------------- close ---------------------------- -->
  <section class="section section--deep">
    <div class="wrap-narrow close">
      <p class="eyebrow">What it costs</p>
      <h2 class="close__h">Nothing, and we mean the whole thing.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The 45 minutes and the report are both free, and both yours to keep. We
        do it because it is the most honest way to be judged: on the quality of
        the thinking, with the sources attached. If we go on to build together,
        we say what it would take. If we don&rsquo;t, you still know the one
        thing we&rsquo;d do first, and why.
      </p>
      <div class="close__ctas">
        <a href="#request" class="btn btn--on-deep">Book the call</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* Local to this page. Shared primitives live in styles/tokens.css. */
    .hero { padding-block: clamp(var(--sp-16), 10vw, var(--sp-24)) var(--sp-16); }
    .hero__in { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-5); }
    .hero__h {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 6.5vw, var(--text-6xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: 0;
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .hero__em { color: var(--accent); }
    .hero__lede { max-width: 58ch; margin: 0; }
    .hero__cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-3); margin-top: var(--sp-2); }

    .h2 {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-2xl), 3.6vw, var(--text-4xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: var(--sp-3) 0 var(--sp-5);
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .h2 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }
    .section--deep .h2 { color: #fff; }

    .head { max-width: 60ch; margin-bottom: var(--sp-10); }
    .head .lede { margin: 0; }

    .body {
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
      color: var(--ink-2);
      max-width: 60ch;
      margin: 0 0 var(--sp-5);
    }
    .body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .cards {
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: card;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--sp-5);
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    }
    .card {
      counter-increment: card;
      position: relative;
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: var(--sp-6);
    }
    .card::before {
      content: counter(card, decimal-leading-zero);
      font-family: var(--font-accent);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--accent);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    }
    .card__h {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      line-height: var(--lh-snug);
      margin: var(--sp-2) 0 var(--sp-3);
    }
    .card__b { font-size: var(--text-md); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }

    .two { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-8); }
    @media (min-width: 48rem) {
      .two { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--sp-10); }
    }

    /* Mirrors how a declared blank renders inside the report itself. */
    .blankdemo {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.9em;
      color: var(--accent-deep);
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0 0;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    /* The process steps: numbered, because the order is the point. */
    ol.steps {
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: st;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--sp-8);
      max-width: var(--page-narrow);
    }
    .step { counter-increment: st; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2); position: relative; padding-left: var(--sp-10); }
    .step::before {
      content: counter(st);
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-accent);
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: 1.1;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    .step__h { font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight); margin: 0; }
    .step__b { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: var(--lh-body); max-width: 62ch; }

    .close { display: grid; gap: var(--sp-5); justify-items: start; }
    .close__ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-5); align-items: center; }
    .close__h {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: var(--lh-tight);
      letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
      margin: 0;
      color: #fff;
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
